==Battleground==
*2 [[Heavenly Hippoe]]s spawn after 16.67 seconds<sup>500f</sup>, delay 5~10 seconds<sup>150f~300f</sup>.
*1 [[Angelic Gory]] spawns after 50 seconds<sup>1,500f</sup>.
*5 [[Gabriel]]s spawn after 60 seconds<sup>1,800f</sup>, delay 3.33~6.67 seconds<sup>100f~200f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Gabriel]]s spawn after 166.67 seconds<sup>5,000f</sup>, delay 20~33.33 seconds<sup>600f~1,000f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**Infinite [[Gabriel]]s spawn, delay 13.33~26.67 seconds<sup>400f~800f</sup>.
**5 [[Gabriel]]s spawn, delay 3.33~6.67 seconds<sup>100f~200f</sup>.
**1 [[Sunfish Jones]] spawns.
**1 [[Divine Cyclone]] spawns as the boss.

==Strategy==
Since the previous stage only required 3-4 cats (including [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]]), the remaining slots can be used for this stage. Just bring 3 meatshields (preferably including [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Artist Cat/Ramen Cat]]), [[Bishop Cat (Rare Cat)|Sanzo Cat]] with its Target Angel [[Talents|Talent]], damage dealers (any unit with 250+ range), and perhaps an [[:Category:Anti-Angel Cats|anti-Angel unit]] with the Freeze ability such as [[Juliet Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Juliet Cat]]. If you use [[A Gift of Cats (Rare Cat)|A Gift of Cats]], you'll have to clear the peons first.

A possible lineup would be [[Crazed Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Macho Cat]], [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Wall Cat]], Artist Cat/Ramen Cat, Awakened Bahamut Cat, Princess Juliet Cat/Juliet the Maiko, [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris Cat]]/[[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Dragon Cat]], [[Bishop Cat (Rare Cat)|Sanzo Cat]], and [[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman Cat]] (for the previous stage).

All you have to do is stall the first peons with meatshields and start stacking Sanzos and Juliets. Upgrade your [[Worker Cat]] to level 3 or 5 and once you have enough money, continue the push towards the base until Divine Cyclone appears. Let it advance at least 1/4 or 1/3 of the stage until Sunfish Jones spawns. This way, Sunfish Jones will only hit your meatshields while your debuffers are safe behind them. The long-ranged attackers will kill the perma-frozen Divine Cyclone. Sunfish Jones is easy after that as the enemy base has low HP.

Do not use [[:Category:Cats with Knockback ability|Knockbackers]] (e.g. [[Stilts Cat (Rare Cat)|Stilts Cat]]) for this strategy as they will expose your other debuffers to Sunfish Jones's attacks.

==Trivia==
*Acts of Cat-God's Japanese name (天変地異 ''Tenpenchii'') is an idiom that refers to a catastrophic natural disaster, but contains 天, a kanji meaning heaven/sky.

